<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §1 — the one content instance.

    Band semantics (this build's own resolution of the spec's "composite band
    0-4 = f(goodwill, irritation)", not literally specced): 0 = calmest (one
    warm-drone layer), rising one hum layer per band, band 4 (the last
    threshold, >= 80 composite) is the WORST band and goes SILENT — the
    sheet's own "when the hum drops, stop moving" tell. composite =
    irritation - goodwill*0.5, clamped 0-100; goodwill is LIVE faction-13
    (Forsaken/Forgotten Arsenal) player goodwill, read every check, never
    duplicated into savedata here.

    Numbers below are the kit spec's own "INVENTED parameters (owner tunes)"
    line for §1, carried over verbatim: decay half-life 1 day, thresholds
    10/30/55/80, conversion -1 per 4h at the worst band capped -5/day,
    commentary cooldown 12h.
  -->

  <RimMandrake.Utinni.RustCathedralHum.RM_BiomeAttitudeDef>
    <defName>RUT_RustCathedralAttitude</defName>
    <targetBiome>RUT_RustCathedral</targetBiome>

    <bandThresholds>
      <li>10</li>
      <li>30</li>
      <li>55</li>
      <li>80</li>
    </bandThresholds>
    <bandHysteresisMargin>6</bandHysteresisMargin>
    <goodwillCompositeWeight>0.5</goodwillCompositeWeight>

    <irritationDecayHalfLifeDays>1</irritationDecayHalfLifeDays>
    <checkIntervalTicks>250</checkIntervalTicks>

    <worstBandGoodwillTickIntervalHours>4</worstBandGoodwillTickIntervalHours>
    <worstBandGoodwillTickAmount>-1</worstBandGoodwillTickAmount>
    <worstBandGoodwillCapPerDay>-5</worstBandGoodwillCapPerDay>

    <commentaryCooldownHours>12</commentaryCooldownHours>

    <humLayers>
      <li>RUT_HumLayerDrone</li>
      <li>RUT_HumLayerTense</li>
      <li>RUT_HumLayerAlarm</li>
    </humLayers>

    <!--
      Register law (sheet §6): every line here is §P. Ban 1 (no §GM truth) —
      nothing below names goodwill, irritation, a band number, or the
      Sentinels' faction status. Ban 2 (no mercy explanation) — nothing
      explains WHY the hum calms or WHY it's angry, only what the droid
      itself feels: confusion and fear, the sheet's own named exception to
      that ban. Ban 6 (no deep-drill explanation) is not engaged here at all
      (§5 territory) — nothing below mentions drilling or depth.

      First-pass lines, reversible on one edit — not the owner's authored
      prose, just enough to prove the mechanism fires with real text instead
      of a stub.
    -->
    <commentary>
      <li>
        <band>1</band>
        <lines>
          <li>The droid's tone shifts, almost too low to hear. It doesn't say why.</li>
          <li>Something in the walls just changed pitch. The droid noticed before you did.</li>
        </lines>
      </li>
      <li>
        <band>2</band>
        <lines>
          <li>"That second tone," the droid says. "That one is new. I don't like that one."</li>
          <li>The droid stops what it's doing and listens. It doesn't start again for a while.</li>
        </lines>
      </li>
      <li>
        <band>3</band>
        <lines>
          <li>"Three tones now." The droid's voice has gone flat. "I would like to stop soon."</li>
          <li>The droid backs itself against a wall, facing outward, and stays there.</li>
        </lines>
      </li>
      <li>
        <band>4</band>
        <lines>
          <li>The hum just stopped. The droid isn't moving either. "Why have you angered this place?" it asks no one.</li>
          <li>Total silence, all at once. The droid says nothing at all -- which is worse.</li>
        </lines>
      </li>
    </commentary>
  </RimMandrake.Utinni.RustCathedralHum.RM_BiomeAttitudeDef>

</Defs>
